<section class="shell questions section-space" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
  <h2 id="questions-title">A few things to know.</h2>
  <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article><h3>Does it replace Caffeine?</h3><p>For keeping your Mac awake, yes. Barista uses native macOS power assertions, with timed and indefinite sessions, login startup, and a global shortcut.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Which icons hide?</h3><p>Icons you arrange to the left of &gt; hide together. Icons on the right stay visible. Click &lt; to reveal the group.</p><a class="site-link" href="/docs/config">Read the grouping requirements ↗</a></article>
    <article><h3>What about macOS overflow?</h3><p>macOS controls overflow when revealed icons do not fit. Barista’s arrow hides and reveals the group you arrange to its left.</p></article>
    <article><h3>How do the editions differ?</h3><p>The sandboxed Mac App Store edition provides keep-awake, timers, shortcuts and login settings. Grouping and the GitHub updater belong to the direct edition. Store distribution requires Apple’s review.</p><a class="site-link" href="/docs/releasing">Editions and release status ↗</a></article>
